## 1. The project in one minute

| | |
|---|---|
| **Name** | Tap A Ride ("Taparide"), descriptor "Abuja Smart Mobility Platform", tagline "Ride • Connect • Go" |
| **What it is** | A multi-tenant transport platform. We do not own vehicles; we are the software every operator, fleet owner and the government plugs into, and every rider uses |
| **Where** | Abuja (FCT) first, then other Nigerian cities with state bus fleets |
| **Why now** | ATDEW 2026 (Abuja Tech and Digital Economy Week), themed "Energising Smart Mobility: Powering Cities of the Future". National Innovation Challenge pitch: 24–26 November 2026 |
| **Live app** | https://taparide.vercel.app |
| **Code** | github.com/lozentrad3s/Taparide |
| **Built with** | Flutter (Dart) for web and Android, Supabase (Postgres) for data and sign-in, Vercel serverless functions (Node.js) for AI, maps and keys, Gemini and Claude for AI |
| **One-line pitch** | Abuja has the terminals and the buses. We are the system that runs them. |

---

## 2. The problem we solve

Abuja has no structured, reliable mass transit. Most of its roughly 4.3 million residents depend on informal minibuses, taxis, tricycles and expensive ride-hailing. Every point below comes from Nigerian news reporting gathered in our concept brief (`project_brief_extracted.txt`).

| Pain point | What people report |
|---|---|
| Transport eats income | Some residents spend up to half their income on daily commuting (Daily Trust) |
| Fares change without warning | Fares jump at peak hours, when it rains, and with fuel and park levies |
| "One chance" robberies | Commuters at night cannot tell which taxis are registered; many criminal vehicles use fake plates |
| Stranded at night | Long queues at Berger, Area 1, AYA, Nyanya, Wuse, Gwarinpa and Kubwa as drivers stop early |
| No information | No published routes, schedules or proper bus stops |
| Good services go unused | The electric airport shuttle struggles because of awareness, routes and waiting time |
| Cash friction | Hunting for change; bank transfers fail when the network is poor |

**The real gap is software, not vehicles.**

- **Idle infrastructure.** The FCTA built modern terminals (Mabushi, Kugbo, Federal Secretariat) that sit unused, waiting for operators under a public-private partnership.
- **New fleets, no shared system.** The airport electric shuttle, the Renewed Hope electric buses for civil servants, Abuja Metro rail, CNG buses and private taxis each sell tickets their own way, or only in cash.
- **The investor trust gap.** A person who buys a ₦10 million car and hires a driver only knows what the driver reports. Under-remittance is common, so private investment stays away.
- **No proof of safety.** A rider has no easy way to check at the roadside that a vehicle is registered.

---

## 3. The solution

One platform with five faces:

1. **Rider app.** Search routes, see the fixed fare and the next departures, book a seat, pay by tap card or QR, get a boarding pass, share the trip, and see that the vehicle is verified.
2. **Operator dashboard.** Routes, fares, vehicles, drivers, bookings and revenue for a bus company, shuttle or rail operator.
3. **Fleet-owner dashboard.** What each vehicle earns, per day and per route, which ends the under-remittance problem.
4. **Driver dashboard.** For approved private drivers: go online, see the current ride, complete it, track earnings.
5. **FCTA (government) dashboard.** Ridership, a verified-vehicle register, route activity and an audit trail.

Plus platform-wide services:

- **Partner registration** with an AI pre-check of driver's licence and vehicle papers before an FCTA reviewer approves.
- **Tag Along.** Verified professionals share rides home with colleagues who live nearby, on a cost-sharing basis.
- **Electric vehicles.** Book EV rides with live battery and range, and find charging stations.
- **Tapi**, a 3D mascot and AI ride assistant that plans trips, books seats and tells you when to leave.
- **FindMe AI**, our sister project, gives the smart safety map: nearby places, live traffic, incidents and SOS.
- **Master control centre** for the platform owner, with full analytics across the whole network.

**Product principles** (from `taparide_flutter/PRODUCT.md`):

1. Fixed and visible: fares, times and verification are always shown before a rider commits.
2. One booking, every view: a rider's booking shows up in the operator, fleet and FCTA views.
3. Cashless by default: tap card and QR are the main payment paths.
4. Safety is a feature: verification and trip sharing are never hidden.
5. Honest data: demo figures are labelled; nothing implies an endorsement that does not exist.

