## 4. Who uses it and what they get

| Role | Lands on | Can do | Pain point answered |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Passenger** | Rider home | Search, book, pay, cancel (refund), top up, Tag Along, EV rides, reminders, assistant | Unpredictable fares, no information, cash friction, safety fears |
| **Transport operator** | Operator dashboard | Edit own fares, manage own vehicles, see own bookings and revenue, AI insights | Revenue leakage, empty seats, no demand data |
| **Private driver** (operator role, private-driver provider) | Driver dashboard | Go online, complete rides, see earnings and where riders are | Finding riders, getting paid fairly |
| **Fleet owner** | Fleet dashboard | See owned vehicles, earnings per vehicle, set vehicle status | Under-remittance, no trust, no investment |
| **Government / FCTA** | FCTA dashboard | Approve providers and partner applications, verify vehicles, see all data, audit log | One-chance crime, idle terminals, no planning data |
| **Platform admin** | Master control centre | Everything: suspensions, approvals, role changes (except admin accounts), platform analytics | Running the whole network |

Each role only sees and changes what it is allowed to. This is enforced in the database, not just by hiding buttons (see [Security](#11-security)).

