## 9. The database

Postgres on Supabase. **11 tables, every one with row-level security switched on.**

| Table | Holds |
|---|---|
| `profiles` | Each user's name, phone, organisation, role and linked provider |
| `wallets` | Tap-card number and balance (demo starter balance ₦2,500) |
| `providers` | Operators, fleet owners, rail, EV companies, private drivers; verification status |
| `routes` | Route stops, fixed fare, departure times, provider |
| `vehicles` | Plate, type, capacity, status, verification, earnings, battery for EVs |
| `bookings` | Every trip: who, route or vehicle, seat, fare, ticket code, status |
| `shared_rides` | Tag Along rides and seat requests |
| `charging_stations` | EV charging points and free ports |
| `partner_applications` | Partner sign-ups, documents and the AI check result |
| `audit_log` | Who did what and when |
| `metric_baselines` | Figures for the FCT register not yet on the platform, so dashboards show the whole city honestly |

**Business actions are SQL functions** (all `security definer`, each re-checks the caller's role):
`book_transit`, `book_electric`, `cancel_booking`, `complete_ride`, `top_up`, `offer_shared_ride`, `request_shared_ride`, `settle_tag_along_requests`, `submit_partner_application`, `review_partner_application`, `set_provider_status`, `set_vehicle_verification`, `set_vehicle_status`, `update_route_fare`, `register_vehicle`, `set_user_role`, `log_action`.
Helpers: `my_role`, `my_provider`, `is_staff`, `manages`, `provider_is_verified`, `handle_new_user` (creates the profile and wallet on sign-up).

**Migrations** in `taparide_flutter/supabase/migrations/`, applied in order:

1. `20261016000000_taparide_schema.sql`: tables, security rules, booking and admin functions
2. `20261017000000_partner_registration.sql`: partner applications and review
3. `20261020000000_driver_rides.sql`: private-driver `complete_ride`
4. `20261022000000_protect_admins.sql`: admin accounts can only be changed by the platform owner

`deploy/scripts/supabase-setup.mjs` applies migrations (tracked, so it is safe to re-run), loads the seed data, and creates the demo sign-in accounts.

---

## 10. AI features

AI is used where it saves riders time or operators money, never as decoration.

| Feature | Who | What it does | Where |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Tapi, the ride assistant** | Riders and partners | Plain-language trip planning and actions through tools: `search_routes`, `get_departures`, `book_seat`, `cancel_trip`, `list_my_trips`, `wallet_balance`, `list_electric_cars`, `book_electric_ride`, `list_tag_along_rides`, `plan_road_trip`, `open_findme_map`, `set_reminder`; for partners `dashboard_summary`, `route_performance`, `list_vehicles` | `features/assistant/`, `api/assistant.js` |
| **Offline quick answers** | Riders | Common questions (balance, next bus) answered on the device without calling the AI | `offline_assistant.dart` |
| **Travel Smart suggestions** | Riders | Learns weekday habits from trip history and suggests booking early; "leave by" reminders | `core/insights.dart`, `core/reminders.dart` |
| **AI insights (AI analyst)** | Operators, fleet owners, FCTA, admin | Written summary of the partner's own figures: what changed, where demand is, what to do | `features/portal/insights_page.dart`, `api/insights.js` |
| **Document pre-check** | FCTA reviewers | Reads licence and vehicle papers, compares them with the form, flags mismatches | `api/verify-documents.js` |
| **Demand map** | Drivers, operators | Busiest areas and hours across Abuja | `features/portal/` |
| **Tapi, the 3D mascot** | Everyone | three.js character with moods (wave, think, celebrate, sleep); tap it to open the assistant | `web/mascot/mascot.js`, `shared/mascot/` |

**How the AI layer is built** (`deploy/api/_lib/ai.js`): two providers behind one interface. `AI_PROVIDER=gemini` is the default (newest "flash" model chosen automatically); Claude (`claude-opus-5-5` by default) is the alternative and fallback. Conversation history is kept in each provider's native format so tool calls stay valid. Only signed-in users from our own site can call the AI endpoints, with a per-IP rate limit.

---

## 11. Security

| Layer | What protects it |
|---|---|
| **Data access** | Row-level security on all 11 tables: a rider sees only their own bookings, an operator only their company's, anonymous visitors see nothing |
| **Data changes** | Every write goes through a SQL function that re-checks the caller's role and writes the audit log; there are no direct update permissions on profiles |
| **Admin accounts** | No one can promote a user to admin or change an admin from the app; only the platform owner can, directly in the database. A shared demo admin therefore cannot lock out the master |
| **Master admin** | Private account, not listed on the login page. In demo mode only a salted SHA-256 hash ships in the app, never the password |
| **Secret keys** | Gemini, Claude, CARTO, and the database URL live in the git-ignored `.env.local` and in Vercel as "sensitive" (encrypted, hidden) variables. The browser only ever gets the public Supabase anon key |
| **API endpoints** | Allow-list of our own origins (other sites get "403 forbidden"); signed-in Supabase session required for AI; per-IP rate limit |
| **Map tile proxy** | Only serves the Abuja region, so it can't be used as a free tile server |
| **Browser headers** | HSTS, `X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN`, a restrictive Content-Security-Policy, `nosniff`, a strict referrer policy, and a Permissions-Policy that limits camera, microphone and location |
| **Checks we run** | A secret-pattern scan of every published file and the git history, `npm audit` (0 vulnerabilities), and REST tests that confirm each role's access |
| **Tooling** | `check-keys.mjs` tests every key against its real service and prints PASS/FAIL only; `sync-vercel-env.mjs` sends keys over stdin and never prints them |

Environment variables (names only): `SUPABASE_URL`, `SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`, `SUPABASE_DB_URL` (setup only, never sent to Vercel), `AI_PROVIDER`, `GEMINI_API_KEY`, `GEMINI_MODEL`, `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `ANTHROPIC_MODEL`, `CARTO_API_KEY`, `CARTO_LDS_TOKEN`, `CARTO_GEOCODING`, `EXTRA_ORIGINS`. Master admin: `MASTER_ADMIN_EMAIL`, `MASTER_ADMIN_PASSWORD` (in `.env.master.local`).

---

## 12. Testing and quality

- **Flutter tests** (`taparide_flutter/test`, 19 tests): booking flows, permission rules ("backend enforces roles, not just the UI"), a booking reaching the FCTA figures, insufficient balance and suspended providers, partner registration and driver rides. Run `flutter test`.
- **Screenshot renders** (`test/screens`) produce review images of every screen.
- **Live end-to-end tests** with Playwright click the real site at phone and desktop sizes: rider sign-in, Tapi open/close, Tap & Pay, booking, FindMe map, operator report download, driver dashboard, master control centre, partner applications.
- **Static analysis** with `flutter analyze` and `flutter_lints`.

---

## 13. Running, building and deploying

**Requirements:** the Flutter SDK in a path without spaces (for example `C:\src\flutter`), Node.js 20+, and the Vercel CLI for deployment.

```bash
# Run the app locally (demo backend, no keys needed)
cd taparide_flutter
flutter pub get
flutter run -d chrome

# Run the tests
flutter test

# Check every key in .env.local (prints PASS/FAIL only)
cd deploy && node scripts/check-keys.mjs

# Set up or update the live database (migrations, seed data, demo accounts)
node scripts/supabase-setup.mjs

# Build the web app into deploy/public (live on Supabase when the database is ready)
node scripts/build-web.mjs

# Copy server-side keys to Vercel as sensitive variables
node scripts/sync-vercel-env.mjs

# Deploy to production
npx vercel deploy --prod --scope lozen-s-projects
```

**Hosting:** Vercel project `taparide` under `lozen-s-projects`, at https://taparide.vercel.app. The web build self-hosts its rendering engine (CanvasKit) instead of loading it from Google's CDN, which proved unreliable during testing.

**Never commit:** `.env*` files, `flutter/`, `build/`, `deploy/public/`, `node_modules/`, `test/screens/out/`, `taparide_video/out/`, `public/music/`.

